course: dictionary
lesson: 4451
title: Blended words: hangry
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A blend is a new word made by joining parts of two other words. «Hangry» blends hungry and angry, so it mixes the feeling of being hungry with the feeling of being cross.
explain: Read the words around it to work out its meaning. «I missed lunch and I'm so hangry» tells you the speaker is hungry and cross at the same time. Hangry means bad-tempered because you are hungry.
explain: People often use «hangry» as a light-hearted excuse. «Sorry I snapped, I'm a bit hangry» blames hunger instead of the person for the bad mood. It is a joke, so it is informal, the kind of word you use with friends.
fact: «Hangry» is a blend of hungry and angry.
fact: A blend joins parts of two words to make a new word, like brunch (breakfast + lunch).
fact: «Hangry» means bad-tempered or irritable because you are hungry.
fact: «Hangry» is informal and humorous, so use it when chatting, not in formal writing.
fact: As an excuse, «hangry» is a light-hearted way of saying you are grumpy.
exercise: «Ben missed lunch and was snapping at everyone. He was hangry.» What does hangry mean? | Excited about a trip to the park | *Bad-tempered because he is hungry | Very tired from running | Full up after a big meal
exercise: Which two words are blended to make hangry? | *hungry and angry | happy and angry | hairy and angry | hot and dry
exercise: Which of these is also a blend? | *brunch | dinner plate | breakfast | lunchtime
test: Mum says, «Have a snack, you're getting hangry.» What is she saying? | You have eaten too much cake | You are very happy and full of energy | You need to sleep for longer | *You are cross because you are hungry
test: Why might someone say «I'm hangry» instead of «I'm grumpy»? | To say they are very happy | *To blame hunger, and make it sound light-hearted | To ask for a longer school day | To show they are a famous chef
exam: «Hangry» is an informal word. What does informal mean? | Very old and from long ago | *Relaxed, the kind of word you use with friends, not in formal writing | Only used by scientists in labs | Written in a foreign language
